A CONTINUATION MAY HOLD MORE THAN ONE PARAGRAPH, AND THEY STAY APART.

Everything after the nested list is ONE continuation, not one per paragraph.
Its text holds both paragraphs with a blank line between them, exactly as an
unsplit item does.

Two things could go wrong and this case catches both. Run the paragraphs
together and the last word of the first welds onto the first word of the
second. Give the blank line the content indent and it becomes trailing
whitespace on an otherwise empty line.

The blank line is written bare, which is why the writer tests for an empty
line before it reaches for the indent. The order of those two tests is the
whole of the behaviour here, and it also decides the fate of an item that is
nothing but a checkbox, which is a first line that is legitimately empty; see
`format-keeps-an-item-that-is-only-a-checkbox`.
